body:
External template library by path: a deck's template library draws on a library directory that lives outside the deck. `kalide.yaml` sets the optional top-level key `templates:` to a path naming that external library directory; that directory has exactly the same fixed layout as a local `templates/` (templates-dir-layout) and the layout itself is unchanged — only its root is resolved. A deck uses the external library together with its own deck-root `templates/` directory: the two are library layers that merge into the deck's one template library (layered-template-library). The external layer is loaded when the key is present, the local layer whenever the deck-root `templates/` directory exists, and both when both are present. A library is load-valid with no templates and no themes: nothing beyond `library.yaml` plus that layout structure is required. A deck, however, always resolves a theme — `theme` is optional and defaults to `default` (deck-config, theme-selection) — against the merged library, and an unresolvable theme is an error; so a library that is to host a deck provides the deck's theme (the `default` theme is sufficient), and a deck whose merged library has no matching theme fails validation. Path semantics: a relative path is resolved against the deck root (the directory holding `kalide.yaml`), for portability; an absolute path is allowed; a path above the deck root (e.g. `../shared-lib`) is allowed. A configured path that is missing or not a valid library is a templates error naming the path (templates-dir-required); when the key is absent and there is no local `templates/`, the error names the expected local `templates/`. Each layer's files are used with that layer's root (load, validate, render, serve, the `kalide templates` gallery and live reload), always through the template-library-loader, and an error names the offending file's on-disk path in its OS's native canonical form (native-display-paths). The configured `templates:` value is captured at `kalide start` startup and the resolved external root is pinned to it for the life of that session: a mid-session change stops serving the deck and shows the full-page restart-required error (the `/templates` gallery and the library media/theme routes are pinned at startup and keep serving the startup library; see template-retarget-requires-restart) — while edits of files under either resolved root keep live-reloading. kalide is local-filesystem only: the user supplies the directory and kalide references it by path, with no cloning, fetching or other acquisition (this realizes global.constraint.template-library-shareable and global.constraint.anonymous-install). `kalide init` can point a new deck at an external library — explicitly by `kalide init <path>`, or by the configured user-level default when no path is given (default-template-dir, init-library-resolution) — validating the library AND the deck's theme against it before writing; `kalide init-library <path>` creates a new library that seeds a minimal `default` theme so a defaulted deck resolves (see cli-init, init-library).

AC:
- a deck with `templates: ../shared-lib` and no local `templates/` loads, validates, serves and lists in `kalide templates` from `../shared-lib`, and live-reloads edits made under `../shared-lib`;
- a deck with `templates: ../shared-lib` and a deck-root `templates/` loads both layers: the merged library holds the templates, themes and media of `../shared-lib` and of the local `templates/`, and an edit under either root live-reloads;
- while `kalide start` runs, changing the configured `templates:` value (e.g. `../shared-lib` → `../other-lib`, or adding/removing the key) is not live-applied: the served deck page becomes the full-page error telling the user to restart `kalide start` (the `/templates` gallery and the media/theme routes keep serving the startup library), and serving resumes only after a restart or when the value is edited back to the startup value;
- a deck with neither the key nor a local `templates/` fails (non-zero exit) with a message naming the expected local `templates/` and suggesting `kalide init`;
- a deck whose `templates:` path is missing or is not a valid library (bad/missing `library.yaml`, layout violation) fails with a templates error naming the resolved path;
- a deck whose theme (optional, default `default`) does not resolve in the merged library fails validation (theme-selection);
- `kalide init ../shared-lib` against a library that resolves the deck's theme (default `default`) — which need define no template — writes an empty `slides/`, empty `assets/` and `kalide.yaml` (with `templates: ../shared-lib`), no local `templates/` and no starter slide, and `kalide start` validates and serves from `../shared-lib` (the deck's slide set may be empty); `kalide init ../bad-lib` (invalid library, or a library that does not resolve the deck's theme) fails before writing anything;
- with a configured `default-template-dir` that is a valid library, `kalide init` (no path) writes an external-library deck referencing it, and a configured default that is missing or does not resolve the deck's theme fails before writing anything.
